From: thunder
Subject: [PATCH] dts: mt6833: drive the vibration motor with regulator-haptic

The motor is powered by the VIBR LDO of the MT6359P. The vendor driver
(mediatek,vibrator, its node comes from the factory dtbo) only switches the
LDO and exposes Android's "vibrator" LED, which feedbackd does not use:
feedbackd wants a force-feedback input device. regulator-haptic, the
mainline driver for exactly this wiring, provides one (FF_RUMBLE, with
FF_PERIODIC emulated by ff-memless), maps the strength to the LDO voltage
and stops the motor on suspend. feedbackd's udev rules already know it by
name.

The voltage range is 2.4 to 3.0 V: 3.0 V is what the vendor driver uses;
the lower bound keeps weak effects felt rather than mapping them to a
voltage that may not spin the motor.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833.dts
@@ -6343,6 +6343,17 @@
 			<0x52a940	0x2900		0x41>,
 			<0x5ea940	0x2900		0x41>;
 	};
+
+	/* thunder: the vibration motor sits on the PMIC's VIBR LDO. The vendor driver
+	 * (mediatek,vibrator, from the factory dtbo) only offers Android's LED interface;
+	 * regulator-haptic gives a force-feedback input device, which feedbackd uses,
+	 * with the strength mapped to the LDO voltage. */
+	haptic {
+		compatible = "regulator-haptic";
+		haptic-supply = <&mt_pmic_vibr_ldo_reg>;
+		min-microvolt = <2400000>;
+		max-microvolt = <3000000>;
+	};
 };
 
 #include "mediatek/mt6359p.dtsi"
